Z||000000||Snowball||07-03-2001||11:41 AM||||I have been looking at a lot of post about engine swaps, the more I read the more confused I get. I can tell that everyone wants something different. I have an 88GT auto and I need to do a rebuild this winter or REPOWER. I'm already upside down in the car so got to watch the cost. I have an old 350 from a truck I could rebuild but it looks like too much money to swap. I'm leaning toward 3800 with 4 speed auto. Has anyone done this, and is it hard? Or should I stay with my stock 3 speed auto? Idea's ???  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||07-03-2001||11:46 AM||||Upgrade to a 3.4L or leave it alone.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||07-03-2001||10:10 PM||||The 93-95 3.4-liter Camaro engine is the cheapest and easiest swap. <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||West Coast Fiero||07-03-2001||10:25 PM||||from us a new 3.4 long block can be had for $2000, misc parts ( plugs, wires - etc ) for about $211, decent clutch for from $107 to $350, or if you have an automatic about $50 to get it serviced ( filter & fluid )<P>so essentialy you are looking at $2500 to $3000 for parts, remember you WILL need either a flexplate or flywheel off of an 88 Fiero, depending on which trans you have ( auto or manual )<P>what is your email, I cand send you a complete price list in Excell format<P><BR>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
